# DemonOS PhantomCore on Garuda Linux Dr460nized (KDE) -- package list.
# Section 1: Garuda Dr460nized, from gitlab.com/garuda-linux/tools/iso-profiles
#   garuda/dr460nized @ 760f824c (Packages-Root, -Desktop-Common, -Desktop, -Mhwd, -Live;
#   ">extra" entries included, ">nonfree_x86_64" (NVIDIA profile) left out). KERNEL = linux-garuda
#   (garuda-tools default). Left out, with reasons:
#     KERNEL-headers: kernel headers only needed for DKMS; dropped with broadcom-wl-dkms to fit the build disk
#     broadcom-wl-dkms: DKMS build at image time needs headers; Broadcom firmware still ships in linux-firmware
#     garuda-dracut-support: conflicts with mkinitcpio; the archiso live initramfs needs mkinitcpio-archiso
#     calamares-garuda: configured for Garuda's own miso/garuda-tools live layout (multi-sfs), which this archiso ISO does not use
#     calamares-branding-garuda: goes with calamares-garuda (Garuda branding); not shipped
#     garuda-tools-base-git: garuda-tools live-session plumbing (miso); archiso provides the live boot instead
#     garuda-live-systemd: garuda-tools live-session units; archiso live units are used instead
#     grub-theme-garuda-live: Garuda live boot-menu theme; replaced by the DemonOS GRUB theme (trademark/branding)
#     grub-theme-garuda-dr460nized: Garuda GRUB theme; replaced by the DemonOS GRUB theme (trademark/branding)
#     garuda-hardware-profile-nvidia: nonfree edition only
#     dracut: Garuda's initramfs generator; with it installed garuda-hooks skips mkinitcpio, but the archiso
#       live initramfs must come from mkinitcpio + mkinitcpio-archiso
#   From the DemonOS list: virtualbox-guest-utils-nox dropped (conflicts with virtualbox-guest-utils, pulled by garuda-hardware-profile-vm).
